  "id": "uncertainty-analysis",
  "term": "uncertainty analysis",
  "definition": "Uncertainty analysis is the study and modeling of how much uncertainty is present in beliefs, estimates, or risk assessments. It is used to examine uncertain outcomes and may include numerical methods to quantify that uncertainty, such as estimating confidence intervals when exact mathematical solutions are unavailable.",
